KEY DESIGN DECISIONS (the "why"):
- Full-context over RAG: gemini-3.5-flash's 1M window holds an entire Google
  Doc, so no embeddings/chunking. ContentCache builds one labelled context blob
  (per-tab "## title / URL / body") once per TTL cycle.
- Explicit Gemini cache with inline fallback: caches.create is only viable at
  >= 4096 input tokens (documented minimum). Below that, or on create failure,
  gemini_cache_name stays None and ChatService sends the context inline via
  system_instruction. Tested both branches + the cache-delete-on-refresh path.
- Structured output: response_schema=ChatAnswer (Pydantic) guarantees
  {answer, sources[]} so source links are always present without string parsing.
- Service-account auth (not API key): an API key cannot read link-shared docs.
  _load_credentials accepts a file path OR inline JSON.

ENVIRONMENT GOTCHA (important for future loops): the pre-commit mypy hook runs
in its OWN venv with additional_dependencies=[types-Flask, sqlalchemy, pydantic,
flask-sqlalchemy] — it has NO pytest or google/genai/limiter stubs. Under strict
mypy that made every @pytest.fixture an "untyped decorator [misc]" error and
FlaskClient a [type-arg] error, even though `mypy src/ --ignore-missing-imports`
(the documented validation) was clean. Fix: a single-source pyproject
[[tool.mypy.overrides]] for module "tests.*" relaxing decorator/generic/return
strictness on test code only. src/ remains fully strict. Also: google-auth
credential factories are untyped, so _load_credentials uses `credentials: Any =
service_account.Credentials` (no env-specific # type: ignore that would be
"unused" in the stub-less pre-commit env).

